.\" Manual page for rdpd(8).  mdoc format.
.Dd May 23, 2026
.Dt RDPD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm rdpd
.Nd Remote Desktop Protocol server
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl df
.Op Fl h Ar host
.Op Fl p Ar port
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the Remote Desktop Protocol server.  It listens for incoming RDP
connections, presents a graphical login screen drawn directly with
RDP drawing orders, authenticates the user, and spawns a fresh
per-user X11 session.  The server speaks RDP natively; there is no
VNC in the stack.
.Pp
This is the
.Sy Phase A
release: the daemon completes the full RDP handshake (TPKT, X.224,
TLS, MCS, license, capability negotiation, finalization) and paints
a solid background.  The login greeter, PAM session spawning, X11
session helper, clipboard channel, and NLA are scaffolded but not
yet implemented; see
.Pa docs/ROADMAP.md
in the source tree.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl d
Enable debug logging.
.It Fl f
Run in the foreground and log to standard error instead of
.Xr syslog 3 .
.It Fl h Ar host
Bind to
.Ar host
instead of all addresses.
.It Fl p Ar port
Listen on
.Ar port
instead of 3389.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/rdpd.conf
Configuration file (see
.Xr rdpd.conf 5 ;
not yet honoured in this release).
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr rdpd.conf 5 ,
.Xr rdp-sessionmgr 8 ,
.Xr rdp-session 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Renaud Allard Aq Mt renaud@allard.it
.Sh BUGS
Phase 0 is the protocol skeleton only; it does not yet accept the RDP
handshake.  See the project roadmap.
